<title>USA: NYC Council OKs FY 1997 budget modification.</title>
<headline>NYC Council OKs FY 1997 budget modification.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New York City Council on Thursday approved the fiscal 1997 budget modification the Giuliani administration proposed on January 30, which included $201 million in new revenues in the city debt service account.</p>
<p>The fiscal year ends June 30.</p>
<p>The Council vote was 46-to-2.</p>
<p>The revenues resulted from increased tax collections of $146 million primarily because of the boom on Wall Street as well as increases in state aid and other revenues.</p>
<p>The modification plan also redistributes $272 million in the expense budget.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
